---
import CourseLayout from "../../layouts/CourseLayout.astro";
import {cases,crew} from "../../data/academy";
import {withBase} from "astro-theme-university/url";
---
<CourseLayout title="The case-file library" description="The operation's sources, rules and people. Every required file is supplied here; no external reading is needed to solve a training exercise." eyebrow="THE ARCHIVE / SOURCES">
<div class="callout"><p><strong>Read the authority, not just the title.</strong> A witness claim, a provisional model and an authoritative revision do different jobs. The archive preserves superseded documents.</p></div>
<nav aria-label="Case-file index"><ol>{cases.map(c=><li><a href={"#"+c.id}>{c.id} — {c.title}</a></li>)}</ol></nav>
{cases.map(c=><article class="case-file" id={c.id}><p class="eyebrow">{c.id} / FIRST USED IN WEEK {c.week}</p><h2>{c.title}</h2><p class="small">{c.authority}</p><p>{c.body}</p>{c.supersedes&&<p><strong>Supersedes:</strong> <a href={"#"+c.supersedes}>{c.supersedes}</a>. The earlier record remains available.</p>}<a href={withBase("/sessions/week-"+String(c.week).padStart(2,"0")+"/")}>Use this file in the lab ↗</a></article>)}
<section id="crew"><h2>The crew dossiers</h2><p>These are participants in the fiction, not the teaching team. Capability, responsibility and consent must be considered separately.</p>{crew.map(c=><article class="staff-row" id={c.id}><span class="staff-mark" aria-hidden="true">{c.name.split(" ").map(w=>w[0]).join("")}</span><div><h3>{c.name} / {c.role}</h3><p>{c.contribution} <strong>Condition:</strong> {c.condition}</p></div></article>)}</section>
<section><h2>How to read the archive</h2><p>An observation reports what a source records. A claim interprets what happened or why. An assumption treats an unsettled condition as true for a decision. Confidence is separate from category. A source can be accurately quoted and still fail to support the conclusion drawn from it.</p><p>Version numbers matter: E03 remains the source for historical R1 runs. E07 governs revised R2 runs. A rehearsal preset explicitly states which version applies.</p></section>
<section><h2>Course-design references</h2><p>These optional references explain the educational structure, rather than the fictional bank. All original case files above were written for MASTERMIND.</p><ul><li><a href="https://callingbullshit.org/syllabus.html">Calling Bullshit</a> carries a clear position through a semester. MASTERMIND carries the distinction between evidence and confidence through its operation.</li><li><a href="https://fab.cba.mit.edu/classes/863.25/">How to Make Almost Anything</a> accumulates capabilities through weekly work. Here the artefacts accumulate into a dossier.</li><li><a href="https://cs007.blog/">CS007</a> makes dated teaching materials directly available. Here every briefing, lab and later-week sample is open.</li><li><a href="https://comp.anu.edu.au/courses/comp1720/lectures/">ANU Art and Interaction Computing</a> uses familiar course navigation. Here thematic names sit beside clear week, lab and assessment labels.</li></ul></section>
</CourseLayout>
